; pd_stub.def - Windows-only. Lists exactly the Pd API symbols csound7_pd.c
; actually calls (confirmed by grepping the source, not guessed), so MSVC's
; librarian (lib.exe, invoked via CMake as ${CMAKE_AR}) can generate a
; minimal pd.lib import library to link against.
;
; Why this exists: a plain `git clone` of pure-data (what
; ../../CMakeLists.txt's FetchContent gets, headers only) does not include
; a pd.lib - that only ships inside the official Pd Windows *release*
; (from puredata.info, not from GitHub - pure-data/pure-data has no GitHub
; Releases at all), alongside a matching pd.dll. Depending on downloading
; that external, version-specific archive during CI would be fragile and
; hard to reproduce. This .def file sidesteps that entirely: real symbol
; resolution only happens later anyway, at runtime, when Pd itself loads
; this DLL into its own process (the exact same reason macOS gets
; `-undefined dynamic_lookup` and Linux needs no flag at all here - MSVC is
; just the one linker of the three that refuses to produce a DLL with any
; unresolved symbol without an explicit stand-in like this).
;
; x64 only (matches every other Windows target in this project) - x64's
; calling convention doesn't decorate extern "C" names, so these plain,
; undecorated names are correct for /MACHINE:X64. Data symbols (plain
; global variables, not functions) are marked DATA - garray_class and
; s_signal are both declared as plain externs in m_pd.h/g_canvas.h, not
; functions, and need that keyword or lib.exe will treat them as code.
;
; UNVERIFIED - no Windows machine available to confirm this actually
; resolves cleanly against a real Pd.exe process. The technique itself
; (generating a stub import lib from a hand-written symbol list, ahead of
; ever having the real DLL) is a standard, well-established Windows
; technique, not something improvised for this project.
LIBRARY "pd"
EXPORTS
    gensym
    class_new
    class_domainsignalin
    class_addmethod
    class_addanything
    class_addlist
    pd_new
    canvas_getcurrent
    canvas_getdir
    atom_getsymbol
    atom_getfloat
    pd_error
    inlet_new
    outlet_new
    outlet_anything
    sys_getsr
    post
    dsp_addv
    pd_findbyclass
    garray_getfloatwords
    garray_redraw
    open_via_path
    class_gethelpdir
    s_signal DATA
    garray_class DATA
